"\n\n\n\n\n## Review\nThis is a place I always visit right after arriving at Busan Station.  \nIt opens at 10:30, and I always arrive around 10:10, take a walk around Busan Station, and do an \"open run\" right away.  \n\nI naturally ordered the mul-milmyeon (cold wheat noodles).  \nBut this time, since I didn't know when I'd visit Busan again, I ordered a double portion out of regret.  \n\nAfter ordering the double portion, I saw noodle refill on the menu and wondered what the difference was while drinking the warm broth they provided.  \nThe broth here is quite well-seasoned, so it's delicious even on its own.  \nI wish I could take it out and drink it like coffee while walking around.  \n\nNot long after, they brought the mul-milmyeon I ordered.  \nThe double portion came in a larger bowl and had more generous portions of noodles and toppings.  \n\nI thought it might be too much, but once I started eating, I finished it in no time.  \nI thought to myself, 'I still eat pretty well.'  \n\nI wished there was a franchise near my house.\n## Pictures\n\n\n\n\n"